{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "WRFPerturbationCoriolis",
  "description": "WRF-ARW's perturbation Coriolis force (pert_coriolis = .true.), SUBROUTINE perturbation_coriolis of dyn_em/module_big_step_utilities_em.F:3854-4171, written as instantaneous decoupled tendencies of a single column on the EarthSciDiscretizations column_nonuniform_1d grid. The horizontal Coriolis terms act on the wind MINUS the base-state (initial-sounding) wind interpolated to the current layer height, so a base wind (u_b, v_b) is in geostrophic balance with an implied large-scale pressure gradient that the column never computes: du/dt = f (v - v_b) - e cos(alpha) w, dv/dt = -f (u - u_b) + e sin(alpha) w, and at the interior interfaces dw/dt = e (cos(alpha) u' - sin(alpha) v') with u' = u - u_b, v' = v - v_b carried onto the interface. In the em_scm_xy reference column (u_b, v_b) = (3, -9) m/s at every level, the geostrophic wind of the case; plain Coriolis on the total wind (pert_coriolis = .false.) gives a different trajectory. f = 2 Omega sin(lat) and e = 2 Omega cos(lat) are consumer-supplied, as are sin/cos of the grid rotation alpha. Discretization as in WRF for a horizontally uniform column: w enters the u and v equations as the arithmetic mean of the two bounding interfaces (0.25 times the four neighbouring rw), u' and v' enter the w equation through the linear-interpolation weights w_above/w_below (WRF fnm/fnp, eta-based; consumer-supplied geometry) and only on the interior interfaces 2..NLEV (kts+1..ktf) -- the surface and top interfaces get no Coriolis term. The base wind is interpolated between the base heights z_base with the clamping of WRF's three-point weights (min(1, max(0, ...))), which is interp.linear's clamping, written with lib/table_interp.esm (the bracket zc_bracket once, then interp_linear_bracketed for each wind component) because the base profile is a run-time table (esm-spec section 9.2 admits only literal const tables in the closed function). Decoupling: in the idealized Cartesian column every map factor is 1 and the hybrid coefficients are c1 = 1, c2 = 0 (hybrid_opt = 0), so the coupling masses of the u, v and w points are all the column dry mass and cancel; the general map-projection / hybrid form is NOT transcribed. Consumer-supplied column fields are rewrite-target ops input_<name>.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": ["wrf", "dynamics", "coriolis", "geostrophic", "column"],
  "references": [
   {"citation": "Skamarock, W. C., et al. (2021). A Description of the Advanced Research WRF Model Version 4.3. NCAR/TN-556+STR, section 2.3 (Coriolis terms) and the pert_coriolis option.", "doi": "10.5065/1dfh-6p97"},
   {"citation": "WRF v4.8.0 dyn_em/module_big_step_utilities_em.F:3854-4171 (perturbation_coriolis), called from dyn_em/module_em.F:747 (rk_tendency)."}
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {"type": "integer", "default": 59, "description": "Number of model layers (WRF kde - 1). Bound into the column grid at the import edge; 59 is the em_scm_xy reference column."}
 },
 "models": {
  "WRFPerturbationCoriolis": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {"ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm", "bindings": {"NLEV": "NLEV"}},
    {"ref": "./column_staggering.esm"},
    {"ref": "../../../lib/table_interp.esm"}
   ],
   "variables": {
    "ze_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Coupling target (assembly input path): a shaped parameter that receives the interface heights, from the column geometry's z_w through a document-level `coupling.variable_map` (`param_to_var`) when an assembly's mount-edge template library lowers `input_ze` to this parameter. Unused in the component's own inline tests, which lower `input_ze` to a dumped profile."},
    "w_above_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Coupling target (assembly input path): a shaped parameter that receives the interface interpolation weight of the layer above (WRF fnm), from the column geometry through a document-level `coupling.variable_map` (`param_to_var`) when an assembly's mount-edge template library lowers `input_w_above` to this parameter. Unused in the component's own inline tests, which lower `input_w_above` to a dumped profile."},
    "w_below_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Coupling target (assembly input path): a shaped parameter that receives the interface interpolation weight of the layer below (WRF fnp), from the column geometry through a document-level `coupling.variable_map` (`param_to_var`) when an assembly's mount-edge template library lowers `input_w_below` to this parameter. Unused in the component's own inline tests, which lower `input_w_below` to a dumped profile."},
    "u_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Coupling target (assembly input path): a shaped parameter that receives the layer zonal wind u from the EqWeather-SCM state document's ODE state (couplings/eqweather_scm_dynamics.esm) through a document-level `coupling.variable_map` (`param_to_var`), when that document's mount-edge library couplings/tests/scmstate_couple_cor_inputs.esm lowers `input_u` to it. Unused in the component's own inline tests, which lower `input_u` to a dumped profile instead."},
    "v_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Coupling target (assembly input path): a shaped parameter that receives the layer meridional wind v from the EqWeather-SCM state document's ODE state (couplings/eqweather_scm_dynamics.esm) through a document-level `coupling.variable_map` (`param_to_var`), when that document's mount-edge library couplings/tests/scmstate_couple_cor_inputs.esm lowers `input_v` to it. Unused in the component's own inline tests, which lower `input_v` to a dumped profile instead."},
    "w_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Coupling target (assembly input path): a shaped parameter that receives the interface vertical velocity w from the EqWeather-SCM state document's ODE state (couplings/eqweather_scm_dynamics.esm) through a document-level `coupling.variable_map` (`param_to_var`), when that document's mount-edge library couplings/tests/scmstate_couple_cor_inputs.esm lowers `input_w` to it. Unused in the component's own inline tests, which lower `input_w` to a dumped profile instead."},
    "f": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1/s", "default": 8.899e-05, "description": "Coriolis parameter 2 Omega sin(lat) (WRF f); default the em_scm_xy column at 37.6 N."},
    "e": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1/s", "default": 0.00011554, "description": "Horizontal Coriolis parameter 2 Omega cos(lat) (WRF e)."},
    "sina": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 0.0, "description": "Sine of the grid rotation relative to true north (WRF sina)."},
    "cosa": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 1.0, "description": "Cosine of the grid rotation (WRF cosa)."},
    "ze": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Interface heights, (phb + ph)/g, through `input_ze`."},
    "u": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Zonal wind on the layers, through `input_u`."},
    "v": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Meridional wind on the layers, through `input_v`."},
    "w": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Vertical velocity on the interfaces, through `input_w`."},
    "u_base": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Base-state zonal wind on the base heights (WRF u_base), through `input_u_base`."},
    "v_base": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Base-state meridional wind (WRF v_base), through `input_v_base`."},
    "z_base": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Base-state layer heights (WRF z_base), through `input_z_base`."},
    "w_above": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Interpolation weight of the layer above each interior interface (WRF fnm), through `input_w_above`."},
    "w_below": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Interpolation weight of the layer below each interior interface (WRF fnp), through `input_w_below`."},
    "zc": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Current layer-centre heights."},
    "zc_bracket": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Lower bracketing index of each current layer height on the base heights (the number of base heights at or below it, held to [1, NLEV-1]); shared by the u and v lookups."},
    "u_b": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Base-state zonal wind at the current layer heights."},
    "v_b": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Base-state meridional wind at the current layer heights."},
    "u_p": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Perturbation zonal wind u - u_b."},
    "v_p": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Perturbation meridional wind v - v_b."},
    "w_c": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Vertical velocity at the layers, the mean of the two bounding interfaces."},
    "u_p_w": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Perturbation zonal wind on the interior interfaces; 0 on the faces."},
    "v_p_w": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Perturbation meridional wind on the interior interfaces; 0 on the faces."},
    "du_dt": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Coriolis tendency of u."},
    "dv_dt": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Coriolis tendency of v."},
    "dw_dt": {"type": "unknown", "units": "m/s^2", "shape": ["lev_nodes"], "description": "Coriolis tendency of w; 0 on the surface and top interfaces."}
   },
   "equations": [
    {"lhs": "ze", "rhs": {"op": "input_ze", "args": []}},
    {"lhs": "u", "rhs": {"op": "input_u", "args": []}},
    {"lhs": "v", "rhs": {"op": "input_v", "args": []}},
    {"lhs": "w", "rhs": {"op": "input_w", "args": []}},
    {"lhs": "u_base", "rhs": {"op": "input_u_base", "args": []}},
    {"lhs": "v_base", "rhs": {"op": "input_v_base", "args": []}},
    {"lhs": "z_base", "rhs": {"op": "input_z_base", "args": []}},
    {"lhs": "w_above", "rhs": {"op": "input_w_above", "args": []}},
    {"lhs": "w_below", "rhs": {"op": "input_w_below", "args": []}},
    {"lhs": "zc", "rhs": {"op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "column_cell_center", "bindings": {"ze": "ze"}}},
    {"lhs": "zc_bracket", "rhs": {"op": "faq", "output_idx": ["k"], "args": [], "ranges": {"k": {"from": "lev"}},
      "expr": {"op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "bracket_index", "bindings": {"axis": "z_base", "x": {"op": "index", "args": ["zc", "k"]}, "n": "NLEV"}}}},
    {"lhs": "u_b", "rhs": {"op": "faq", "output_idx": ["k"], "args": [], "ranges": {"k": {"from": "lev"}},
      "expr": {"op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "interp_linear_bracketed", "bindings": {"table": "u_base", "axis": "z_base", "x": {"op": "index", "args": ["zc", "k"]}, "i_lo": {"op": "index", "args": ["zc_bracket", "k"]}, "n": "NLEV"}}}},
    {"lhs": "v_b", "rhs": {"op": "faq", "output_idx": ["k"], "args": [], "ranges": {"k": {"from": "lev"}},
      "expr": {"op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "interp_linear_bracketed", "bindings": {"table": "v_base", "axis": "z_base", "x": {"op": "index", "args": ["zc", "k"]}, "i_lo": {"op": "index", "args": ["zc_bracket", "k"]}, "n": "NLEV"}}}},
    {"lhs": "u_p", "rhs": {"op": "-", "args": ["u", "u_b"]}},
    {"lhs": "v_p", "rhs": {"op": "-", "args": ["v", "v_b"]}},
    {"lhs": "w_c", "rhs": {"op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "column_cell_center", "bindings": {"ze": "w"}}},
    {"lhs": "u_p_w", "rhs": {"op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "interpolate_to_interfaces", "bindings": {"f": "u_p", "wa": "w_above", "wb": "w_below"}}},
    {"lhs": "v_p_w", "rhs": {"op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "interpolate_to_interfaces", "bindings": {"f": "v_p", "wa": "w_above", "wb": "w_below"}}},
    {"lhs": "du_dt", "rhs": {"op": "-", "args": [{"op": "*", "args": ["f", "v_p"]}, {"op": "*", "args": ["e", "cosa", "w_c"]}]}},
    {"lhs": "dv_dt", "rhs": {"op": "+", "args": [{"op": "*", "args": [{"op": "-", "args": ["f"]}, "u_p"]}, {"op": "*", "args": ["e", "sina", "w_c"]}]}},
    {"lhs": "dw_dt", "rhs": {"op": "*", "args": ["e", {"op": "-", "args": [{"op": "*", "args": ["cosa", "u_p_w"]}, {"op": "*", "args": ["sina", "v_p_w"]}]}]}}
   ],
   "tests": [
     {
       "id": "coriolis_step60",
       "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU gfortran 13.3 REAL*4 build, dt = 60 s, damp_opt = 2 dampcoef = 0.003 zdamp = 5000 m, pert_coriolis = .true., use_theta_m = 1, hybrid_opt = 0; data/eqwefic/scm_dyn, the scm_ref namelist re-run with the instrumented binary) dumped by the ctessum-claude/WRF fork, branch earthsciml-instrumented, commit 83347b2 (dyn_em/module_em.F rk_tendency, rk_step 1 of the step; module_esm_dump), merged with the same step's radiation subassembly dump and the wrfout eta grid by tools/merge_dumps.py into data/eqwefic/dumps/dyn_column/esm_dump_dyn_suite_<step>.json. The rebuilt binary reproduces the archived scm_ref radiation subassembly dumps bit for bit (all but the three B9 variables). The column is horizontally uniform (u, v identical in the two tile columns, ww = 0, all map factors 1, c1 = 1, c2 = 0). Expected tendencies are the dumped mass-coupled increments of the named routine divided by the coupling mass of their grid point (muu, muv, mut), i.e. the instantaneous decoupled rate at the time-level-n state; references are single precision, so tolerances follow the rel 1e-5 real32 convention, with absolute Linf bounds on whole profiles where values pass through zero. Routine: perturbation_coriolis (dyn_em/module_big_step_utilities_em.F:3854-4171). u_base = 3, v_base = -9 m/s at every level (the geostrophic wind of the case). The eta interpolation weights w_above/w_below are the dumped fnm/fnp. Measured residual over the three regimes (zero tolerance): Linf <= 1.2e-10 m/s^2 in du_dt (values <= 5.3e-4), <= 2.5e-11 in dv_dt (<= 2.1e-4), <= 3.1e-11 in dw_dt (<= 2.6e-4). Regime: step 60 (t = 1 h, early afternoon, convective boundary layer).",
       "parameter_overrides": {
         "f": 8.898477972252294e-05,
         "e": 0.00011554911179700866,
         "sina": 0.0,
         "cosa": 1.0
       },
